 "format": "bgsim.subsystem",
 "name": "HeliAirframe",
 "description": "One A109 in calm air (Heffley & Mnich, NASA CR-177476): the rigid body on a free joint with a wrench source per component (main rotor, fuselage, tail rotor, tailplane, fin), the drivetrain as a rotational bond graph, the governor and the air data. Inputs th0, B1, A1, thtr (deg). Pin the start state with Free/qw .. Free/pz, Body/inertia/P, MR/a1, MR/b1, Rotor/P and Gov/xi (default: the hover trim) and the rotor speed the aerodynamics see with MR/rpm_mode and TR/rpm_mode (1 the drivetrain's, 0 the nominal). Generated by design/build_model.py.",
