  "annotations": [
   {
    "id": "a1",
    "kind": "text",
    "text": "**Airframe.** RigidBody3D on its principal axes (the report's Ixz tilts them 10.49 deg from the body x axis). Each component is a modulated wrench source at its own point: ExternalWrenchSpatial bonded through a FixedTransform3DNeutral that carries the offset, so the bond graph forms r x F.",
    "x": 0,
    "y": -100,
    "w": 900,
    "h": 50,
    "color": "blue"
   },
   {
    "id": "a2",
    "kind": "text",
    "text": "**Components** (modulated sources): the report's main rotor (flapping, thrust/inflow), fuselage, tail rotor, tailplane and fin, in SI. Their forces act at the hub, the fuselage point, the tail-rotor hub, the tailplane and the fin.",
    "x": 600,
    "y": 200,
    "w": 600,
    "h": 50,
    "color": "blue"
   },
   {
    "id": "a3",
    "kind": "text",
    "text": "**Drivetrain** (rotational bond graph, ours): the rotor inertia on its 1-junction with the aerodynamic torque; the mast 0-junction (common torque) whose flows make rotor speed = gearbox speed + airframe yaw rate (ShaftAxis, the reaction torque on the airframe); the gearbox 1-junction with the engine torque (Governor), the transmission losses and the tail-rotor gear (TF) to the tail-rotor junction and its torque.",
    "x": 1260,
    "y": 180,
    "w": 900,
    "h": 70,
    "color": "blue"
   }
  ]
 },
